#. SignIn: inline error under the method that failed. Arguments: {method} = a sign-in method's name (Apple, Google, passkey…).
msgid "signIn.methodError"
msgstr "El inicio de sesión con {method} no terminó. Inténtalo de nuevo."

#. Getting a sign-in code…
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser.
msgid "signInHandoff.starting"
msgstr "Obteniendo un código de inicio de sesión…"

#. Scan the code with your phone, or go to {url} and enter this code.
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser. TV and console layout. Arguments: {url} = a web address, shown as is.
msgid "signInHandoff.scan"
msgstr "Escanea el código con tu teléfono, o ve a {url} y escribe este código."

#. Scan the QR code with your phone, or go to this address and enter the code below.
#. SignInHandoff on a TV: the QR code sits beside it and the web address follows on its own line, so the sentence does not repeat it.
msgid "signInHandoff.scanTv"
msgstr "Escanea el código QR con tu teléfono o ve a esta dirección y escribe el código de abajo."

#. Link copied
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser. Confirmation after Copy link.
msgid "signInHandoff.linkCopied"
msgstr "Enlace copiado"

#. Choose Sign in on {device} on the sign-in page to finish.
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser. The hosted approval page ends with a “Sign in on {device}” button, next to Deny; the label stays in English. Arguments: {device} = this device's friendly name.
msgid "signInHandoff.confirm"
msgstr "Elige «Sign in on {device}» en la página de inicio de sesión para terminar."

#. Signed in
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser. Shown for a moment before the product continues.
msgid "signInHandoff.ok"
msgstr "Sesión iniciada"

#. Get a new code
#. SignInHandoff: sign-in continues on another device or in the browser. After the code expired or was refused.
msgid "signInHandoff.newCode"
msgstr "Obtener código nuevo"

#. macos: Get a New Code
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "signInHandoff.newCode"
msgstr "Obtener código nuevo"

#. Enter your license key
#. Activate: license key entry.
msgid "activate.title"
msgstr "Escribe tu clave de licencia"

#. You'll find it in your purchase email.
#. Activate: license key entry.
msgid "activate.lede"
msgstr "La encontrarás en el correo de tu compra."

#. Activate license
#. Activate: license key entry. Submits the key.
msgid "activate.submit"
msgstr "Activar licencia"

#. macos: Activate License
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "activate.submit"
msgstr "Activar licencia"

#. Activate a license
#. Portal: opens the Activate dialog (account menu, Library key tile, empty Library, Missing a license strip).
msgid "common.activateLicense"
msgstr "Activar una licencia"

#. macos: Activate a License
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "common.activateLicense"
msgstr "Activar una licencia"

#. Activating…
#. Activate: license key entry.
msgid "activate.busy"
msgstr "Activando…"

#. {product} is ready
#. ActivateDone: the step after a license key activates. Arguments: {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "activate.done.title"
msgstr "{product} está listo"

#. {tier} · {term} · this {deviceKind} is device {n} of {limit}.
#. ActivateDone: the license line. Arguments: {tier} = the tier's name (never translated), {term} = the term (Lifetime, Renews 3 Mar), {deviceKind} = the device kind already worded (computer, phone), {n} and {limit} = integers.
msgid "activate.done.device"
msgstr "{tier} · {term} · este {deviceKind} es el dispositivo {n} de {limit}."

#. Keep {product} in your account
#. ActivateDone: the quiet recommendation card. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "activate.recommend.title"
msgstr "Conserva {product} en tu cuenta"

#. Recommended
#. ActivateDone: the badge on the recommendation card.
msgid "activate.recommend.badge"
msgstr "Recomendado"

#. Cloud Sync keeps your settings and saves on every device
#. ActivateDone: a reason line, shown only when the product has Cloud Sync. Cloud Sync is a feature name; use the glossary term. The first words are a lead-in; the kit may style them.
msgid "activate.recommend.sync"
msgstr "La sincronización en la nube mantiene tus ajustes y partidas en todos tus dispositivos"

#. Get your license back if you lose the key or this device
#. ActivateDone: a reason line, shown when Identity is on. The first words ("Get your license back") are a lead-in; the kit may style them.
msgid "activate.recommend.recover"
msgstr "Recupera tu licencia si pierdes la clave o este dispositivo"

#. Move it to a new device yourself, without asking {developer}
#. ActivateDone: a reason line, shown when Identity is on. Arguments: {developer} = the developer's name (never translated). The first words ("Move it to a new device") are a lead-in; the kit may style them.
msgid "activate.recommend.devices"
msgstr "Pásala a un dispositivo nuevo tú mismo, sin pedírselo a {developer}"

#. Add your name and email
#. ActivateDone: the recommendation card's action; opens AddToAccount.
msgid "activate.recommend.action"
msgstr "Añade tu nombre y correo"

#. macos: Add Your Name and Email
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "activate.recommend.action"
msgstr "Añade tu nombre y correo"

#. Or continue without an account. {product} works the same.
#. ActivateDone: under the recommendation card. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "activate.recommend.skip"
msgstr "O continúa sin cuenta. {product} funciona igual."

#. Keep your license safe in Polaris Locker
#. ActivateDone: the single reason line when Identity is off; the action opens the portal.
msgid "activate.recommend.portal"
msgstr "Guarda tu licencia a salvo en Polaris Locker"

#. Your license and its devices stay as they are. You'll confirm the email with a code in your browser.
#. AddToAccount: under the name and email fields.
msgid "activate.attach.lede"
msgstr "Tu licencia y sus dispositivos se quedan como están. Confirmarás el correo con un código en tu navegador."

#. We send a code to this email in your browser. {product} never sees it.
#. AddToAccount: the fine print under the email field. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "activate.attach.fine"
msgstr "Enviamos un código a este correo en tu navegador. {product} nunca lo ve."

#. {product} is in your account
#. AddToAccount: added. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "activate.attach.done"
msgstr "{product} está en tu cuenta"

#. Cloud Sync is on for this {deviceKind}. Sign in on your other devices to sync them too.
#. AddToAccount: added, shown only when the product has Cloud Sync. Cloud Sync is a feature name; use the glossary term. Arguments: {deviceKind} = the device kind already worded (computer, phone).
msgid "activate.attach.syncOn"
msgstr "La sincronización en la nube está activada en este {deviceKind}. Inicia sesión en tus otros dispositivos para sincronizarlos también."

#. Couldn't add this license. Try again in a moment.
#. AddToAccount: adding failed on a server error. Not about the email, so the person stays on the form.
msgid "activate.attach.failed"
msgstr "No se pudo añadir esta licencia. Inténtalo de nuevo en un momento."

#. This license was sent to {maskedEmail}. Sign in with that email to keep it in your account.
#. ActivateDone: the license was sent to an email and no account holds it yet. Arguments: {maskedEmail} = the email with its middle hidden, such as a•••@example.com (never translated).
msgid "activate.waiting"
msgstr "Esta licencia se envió a {maskedEmail}. Inicia sesión con ese correo para conservarla en tu cuenta."

#. Sign in as {maskedEmail}
#. ActivateDone: the action under the waiting line. Arguments: {maskedEmail} = the email with its middle hidden (never translated).
msgid "activate.waitingSignIn"
msgstr "Iniciar sesión como {maskedEmail}"

#. macos: Sign In as {maskedEmail}
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "activate.waitingSignIn"
msgstr "Iniciar sesión como {maskedEmail}"

#. This license is in a Polaris Locker account
#. AddToAccount: someone attached the license while this screen was open.
msgid "activate.owned.title"
msgstr "Esta licencia está en una cuenta de Polaris Locker"

#. Sign in with the email it was sent to. {product} starts on this {deviceKind} as soon as you do.
#. AddToAccount: under the owned title. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated), {deviceKind} = the device kind already worded (computer, phone).
msgid "activate.owned.lede"
msgstr "Inicia sesión con el correo al que se envió. {product} arranca en este {deviceKind} en cuanto lo hagas."

#. This license was sent to another email
#. AddToAccount: the license's email does not match the account.
msgid "activate.otherEmail.title"
msgstr "Esta licencia se envió a otro correo"

#. It was sent to {maskedEmail}. Sign in with that email, or add it to this account and verify it.
#. AddToAccount: under the otherEmail title. Arguments: {maskedEmail} = the email with its middle hidden (never translated).
msgid "activate.otherEmail.body"
msgstr "Se envió a {maskedEmail}. Inicia sesión con ese correo, o añádelo a esta cuenta y verifícalo."

#. Verify that email
#. AddToAccount: opens the portal's sign-in methods.
msgid "activate.otherEmail.verify"
msgstr "Verificar ese correo"

#. macos: Verify That Email
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "activate.otherEmail.verify"
msgstr "Verificar ese correo"

#. Not in an account
#. AccountAndLicense: the row for a license held by a key only. Its action is Add your name and email.
msgid "account.notInAccount"
msgstr "No está en una cuenta"

#. Add {product} to your account
#. The sign-in card's header when an app asks to add its license to an account. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "signin.attach.header"
msgstr "Añade {product} a tu cuenta"

#. {product} works the same. Add it to an account any time.
#. License key step: under Continue without an account. Arguments: {product} = the product's name (never translated).
msgid "signin.key.skipNote"
msgstr "{product} funciona igual. Añádelo a una cuenta cuando quieras."

#. Offline activation
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.title"
msgstr "Activación sin conexión"

#. Send this request code to whoever gave you your license.
#. OfflineActivation: step 1; the kit's number marker carries the order.
msgid "offlineActivation.request"
msgstr "Envía este código de solicitud a quien te dio la licencia."

#. Copy code
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.copyCode"
msgstr "Copiar código"

#. macos: Copy Code
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "offlineActivation.copyCode"
msgstr "Copiar código"

#. Code copied
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.codeCopied"
msgstr "Código copiado"

#. Load the activation file you get back, or paste its text.
#. OfflineActivation: step 2; the kit's number marker carries the order.
msgid "offlineActivation.loadHint"
msgstr "Carga el archivo de activación que recibas, o pega su texto."

#. Load file…
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file. Opens a file picker.
msgid "offlineActivation.loadFile"
msgstr "Cargar archivo…"

#. macos: Load File…
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "offlineActivation.loadFile"
msgstr "Cargar archivo…"

#. Paste the activation text here
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file. Placeholder of the paste box.
msgid "offlineActivation.paste"
msgstr "Pega aquí el texto de activación"

#. Activate from file
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.submit"
msgstr "Activar desde archivo"

#. macos: Activate from File
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "offlineActivation.submit"
msgstr "Activar desde archivo"

#. You can also drop the file onto this window.
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.dropHint"
msgstr "También puedes soltar el archivo en esta ventana."

#. Activated from the offline file.
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file.
msgid "offlineActivation.done"
msgstr "Activado con el archivo sin conexión."

#. Load or paste an activation file first.
#. OfflineActivation: activation by exchanging a request code and a response file. Inline error.
msgid "offlineActivation.empty"
msgstr "Primero carga o pega un archivo de activación."

#. Replace a device
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Screen title.
msgid "deviceLimit.title"
msgstr "Reemplazar un dispositivo"

#. Your license is on {used} of {limit, plural, one {# device} other {# devices}}
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Arguments: {used} = how many devices use the license, as a number; {limit} = the license's device limit, as a number.
#. Plural on {limit}.
msgid "deviceLimit.heading"
msgid_plural "deviceLimit.heading"
msgstr[0] "Tu licencia está en {used} de {limit} dispositivo"
msgstr[1] "Tu licencia está en {used} de {limit} de dispositivos"
msgstr[2] "Tu licencia está en {used} de {limit} dispositivos"

#. To use it on {formFactor, select, iphone {this iPhone} ipad {this iPad} mac {this Mac} phone {this phone} tablet {this tablet} computer {this computer} tv {this TV} other {this device}}, replace one. You can add it back later.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Arguments: {formFactor} = the device's form factor; each case is a whole phrase.
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este dispositivo, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor iphone: To use it on this iPhone, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "iphone"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este iPhone, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor ipad: To use it on this iPad, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "ipad"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este iPad, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor mac: To use it on this Mac, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "mac"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este Mac, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor phone: To use it on this phone, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "phone"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este teléfono, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor tablet: To use it on this tablet, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "tablet"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en esta tableta, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor computer: To use it on this computer, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "computer"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en esta computadora, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. formFactor tv: To use it on this TV, replace one. You can add it back later.
msgctxt "tv"
msgid "deviceLimit.lede"
msgstr "Para usarla en este televisor, reemplaza uno. Puedes volver a añadirlo más tarde."

#. Replace {device}?
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Confirm block under the selected device. On macOS the kit wraps {device} in curly quotes. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”.
msgid "deviceLimit.confirmTitle"
msgstr "¿Reemplazar {device}?"

#. {device} signs out of {product} and {thisDevice} takes its place. We'll email you about it.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Confirm block body. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”; {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated); {thisDevice} = the platform phrase for the current device (part.thisDevice, for example “this iPhone”).
msgid "deviceLimit.consequence"
msgstr "Se cerrará la sesión de {product} en {device} y {thisDevice} ocupará su lugar. Te lo notificaremos por correo."

#. Replace and continue
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Primary button.
msgid "deviceLimit.primary"
msgstr "Reemplazar y continuar"

#. macos: Replace and Continue
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "deviceLimit.primary"
msgstr "Reemplazar y continuar"

#. {device} was replaced. {product} is continuing.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”; {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "deviceLimit.removed"
msgstr "Se reemplazó {device}. {product} continúa."

#. {device} couldn't be replaced. Try again.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”.
msgid "deviceLimit.failed"
msgstr "No se pudo reemplazar {device}. Vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Replace a device in your browser. {product} continues when you're done.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Browser mode: the device list is only in the browser. Arguments: {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "deviceLimit.browser"
msgstr "Reemplaza un dispositivo en tu navegador. {product} continuará cuando termines."

#. Open in browser
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Browser mode.
msgid "deviceLimit.openBrowser"
msgstr "Abrir en el navegador"

#. macos: Open in Browser
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "deviceLimit.openBrowser"
msgstr "Abrir en el navegador"

#. Scan the code to replace a device on your phone.
#. DeviceLimit, the Replace a device flow (SIGN-IN.md §3.7): the license is on all its devices. Browser mode on TV and console.
msgid "deviceLimit.scan"
msgstr "Escanea el código para reemplazar un dispositivo desde tu teléfono."

#. Sign out of {product} on another device, then try again.
#. DeviceLimit on the key path when the server sent no link to replace a device: the license is on all its devices, so the fix is to free one first. Arguments: {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "deviceLimit.noManage"
msgstr "Cierra sesión de {product} en otro dispositivo y vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Your devices
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license.
msgid "devices.title"
msgstr "Tus dispositivos"

#. Devices using this license.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license.
msgid "devices.lede"
msgstr "Dispositivos que usan esta licencia."

#. {platform} · last used {when}
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Second line of a device row. Arguments: {platform} = the device's platform name (macOS, Windows, iPhone…); {when} = a relative time already formatted by the platform (“2 days ago”).
msgid "devices.meta"
msgstr "{platform} · usado por última vez {when}"

#. {count, plural, one {# device} other {# devices}}
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Arguments: {count} = a number of items.
#. Plural on {count}.
msgid "devices.count"
msgid_plural "devices.count"
msgstr[0] "{count} dispositivo"
msgstr[1] "{count} de dispositivos"
msgstr[2] "{count} dispositivos"

#. Unnamed device
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. A device with no name.
msgid "devices.unnamed"
msgstr "Dispositivo sin nombre"

#. Rename
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license.
msgid "devices.rename"
msgstr "Cambiar nombre"

#. Device name
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Label of the inline rename field.
msgid "devices.renameLabel"
msgstr "Nombre del dispositivo"

#. Remove
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license.
msgid "devices.remove"
msgstr "Quitar"

#. Remove {device}? It signs out of {product}.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Inline confirm. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”; {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated).
msgid "devices.removeConfirm"
msgstr "¿Quitar {device}? Se cerrará su sesión de {product}."

#. No devices are using this license yet.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license.
msgid "devices.empty"
msgstr "Todavía ningún dispositivo usa esta licencia."

#. Couldn't load your devices.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. The list could not be read; a Try again button follows.
msgid "devices.loadFailed"
msgstr "No se pudieron cargar tus dispositivos."

#. Couldn't rename {device}. Try again.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. A rename was refused. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”.
msgid "devices.renameFailed"
msgstr "No se pudo cambiar el nombre de {device}. Vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Couldn't remove {device}. Try again.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. A removal was refused. Arguments: {device} = a device's friendly name, for example “Maya's MacBook”.
msgid "devices.removeFailed"
msgstr "No se pudo quitar {device}. Vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Manage your devices in your browser.
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Browser mode.
msgid "devices.browser"
msgstr "Administra tus dispositivos en tu navegador."

#. Manage devices
#. Devices: the list of devices using the license. Browser mode; opens the account in the browser.
msgid "devices.manage"
msgstr "Administrar dispositivos"

#. macos: Manage Devices
msgctxt "macos"
msgid "devices.manage"
msgstr "Administrar dispositivos"

#. {product} {version}
#. UpdatePrompt: an app update. Title: the product and the new version. Arguments: {product} = the product's name from ProductIdentity (never translated); {version} = a version string such as 2.4.1.
msgid "update.title"
msgstr "{product} {version}"

#. An update is available
#. UpdatePrompt: an app update. Used when the version is unknown.
msgid "update.availableTitle"
